{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the sum of all the rational terms in the expansion of \\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt[3]{3})^{12}\\), we will use the binomial theorem. The binomial theorem states that:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt[3]{3})^{12} = \\sum_{k=0}^{12} \\binom{12}{k} (\\sqrt{2})^{12-k} (\\sqrt[3]{3})^k\n\\]\n\nWe need to determine which terms in this expansion are rational. A term is rational if both \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) and \\(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\) are raised to integer powers that result in rational numbers. Specifically, \\((\\sqrt{2})^{12-k}\\) is rational if \\(12-k\\) is even, and \\((\\sqrt[3]{3})^k\\) is rational if \\(k\\) is a multiple of 3. Therefore, \\(k\\) must satisfy both conditions: \\(k\\) must be a multiple of 3 and \\(12-k\\) must be even.\n\nLet's list the possible values of \\(k\\):\n\n","prefix_end":737,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,2629,315,678,279,24438,3793,304,279,14461,315,1124,1188,59,26888,90,17,92,488,1124,26888,58,18,15370,18,5410,47822,16,17,11035,701,582,686,990,279,9544,20855,57817,13,576,9544,20855,57817,5302,429,1447,59,9640,11520,26888,90,17,92,488,1124,26888,58,18,15370,18,5410,47822,16,17,92,284,1124,1242,15159,74,28,15,92,47822,16,17,92,1124,6863,316,90,16,17,15170,74,92,19788,26888,90,17,5410,47822,16,17,12646,92,19788,26888,58,18,15370,18,5410,61,74,198,59,2533,1654,1184,311,8253,892,3793,304,419,14461,525,24438,13,362,4647,374,24438,421,2176,1124,11520,26888,90,17,11035,8,323,1124,11520,26888,58,18,15370,18,11035,8,525,9226,311,7546,13430,429,1102,304,24438,5109,13,44763,11,1124,1188,59,26888,90,17,5410,47822,16,17,12646,11035,8,374,24438,421,17767,16,17,12646,57758,374,1496,11,323,1124,1188,59,26888,58,18,15370,18,5410,61,74,57758,374,24438,421,17767,74,57758,374,264,5248,315,220,18,13,15277,11,17767,74,57758,1969,26553,2176,4682,25,17767,74,57758,1969,387,264,5248,315,220,18,323,17767