":"eos","text":"To find the sum of all the rational terms in the expansion of \\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt[3]{3})^{12}\\), we will use the binomial theorem. The binomial theorem states that:\n\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt[3]{3})^{12} = \\sum_{k=0}^{12} \\binom{12}{k} (\\sqrt{2})^{12-k} (\\sqrt[3]{3})^k\n\\]\n\nWe need to determine which terms in this expansion are rational. A term is rational if both \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) and \\(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\) are raised to integer powers that result in rational numbers. Specifically, \\((\\sqrt{2})^{12-k}\\) is rational if \\(12-k\\) is even, and \\((\\sqrt[3]{3})^k\\) is rational if \\(k\\) is a multiple of 3. Therefore, \\(k\\) must satisfy both conditions: \\(k\\) must be a multiple of 3 and \\(12-k\\) must be even.\n\nLet's list the possible values of \\(k\\):\n\n- If \\(k = 0\\), then \\(12 - k = 12\\) (even), so \\(k = 0\\) is valid.\n- If \\(k = 3\\), then \\(12 - k = 9\\) (odd), so \\(k = 3\\) is not valid.\n- If \\(k = 6\\), then \\(12 - k = 6\\) (even), so \\(k = 6\\) is valid.\n- If \\(k = 9\\), then \\(12 - k = 3\\) (odd), so \\(k = 9\\) is not valid.\n- If \\(k = 12\\), then \\(12 - k = 0\\) (even), so \\(k = 12\\) is valid.\n\nThus, the valid values of \\(k\\) are 0, 6, and 12. We now calculate the corresponding terms in the expansion:\n\n1. For \\(k = 0\\):\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{0} (\\sqrt{2})^{12-0} (\\sqrt[3]{3})^0 = 1 \\cdot 2^6 \\cdot 1 = 64\n\\]\n\n2. For \\(k = 6\\):\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{6} (\\sqrt{2})^{12-6} (\\sqrt[3]{3})^6 = \\binom{12}{6} \\cdot 2^6 \\cdot 3^2 = 924 \\cdot 64 \\cdot 9 = 924 \\cdot 576 = 532224\n\\]\n\n3. For \\(k = 12\\):\n\\[\n\\binom{12}{12} (\\sqrt{2})^{12-12} (\\sqrt[3]{3})^{12} = 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 3^4 = 1 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 81 = 81\n\\]\n\nThe sum of all the rational terms is:\n\\[\n64 + 532224 + 81 = 532369\n\\]\n\nThus, the sum of all the rational terms in the expansion of \\((\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt[3]{3})^{12}\\) is \\(\\boxed{532369}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{532369}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:445"}
